  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    A century ago, eating real food, drinking spring water, and spending most of your hours
    outdoors was enough. None of those conditions exist for most adults today. Soil
    micronutrient density has dropped. Tap water is stripped and treated. Indoor work
    blocks the daily sun your endocrine system was built to expect. The result is a slow,
    silent under-supplementation across most of the U.S. adult population — running 60–80%
    of the cofactors needed for optimal cognitive aging, hormonal output, and immune resilience.
  </p>
  <p>
    Vitamin D is the headline deficiency. An estimated 40% of U.S. adults are below 30 ng/mL,
    and far more sit below the optimal 60–80 ng/mL range. But it's far from the only one.
    Magnesium deficiency is nearly universal. Most adults are also light on omega-3, B-complex
    (especially B12 and folate), iodine, zinc, and choline. These deficiencies compound silently —
    suboptimal cognition, mood, sleep, recovery, and immunity all trace back to a depleted micronutrient base.
  </p>
  <p>Chronic micronutrient depletion is a quiet MindSpan tax — the foundational stack below is one of the cheapest levers for closing the gap your score is picking up.</p>

  <h2>The Insulting Behaviors</h2>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>Never having a comprehensive nutrient panel done — guessing at what you're deficient in</li>
    <li>Skipping the foundational stack (D3 + K2, magnesium, omega-3) entirely</li>
    <li>Buying random one-off supplements seen on social media, with no protocol or testing</li>
    <li>Taking poor-quality supplements (oxide forms of magnesium, synthetic folic acid instead of methylfolate, low-dose D3 without K2)</li>
    <li>Eating processed and convenience food daily without compensating for the nutrient stripping</li>
    <li>Drinking municipal tap water without filtration AND without any mineral replenishment</li>
    <li>Working indoors year-round with no morning sun exposure or vitamin D supplementation</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-eliminate">Eliminate the Insulting Behavior</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Get a baseline nutrient panel</h3>
      <p>Test before guessing — 25-OH vitamin D, RBC magnesium, omega-3 index, B12 + folate + homocysteine, ferritin, zinc, iodine. Without data, you're guessing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Run the foundational stack</h3>
      <p>D3 (5,000–10,000 IU/day with K2-MK7), magnesium glycinate or threonate (300–600 mg), high-EPA omega-3 (2 g+/day), methylated B-complex.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Get morning sun, daily</h3>
      <p>Direct sun on skin within 30 minutes of waking. 5–10 minutes anchors circadian rhythm; 20–30 minutes at midday delivers vitamin D when latitude allows.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Fix the foundational basics first</h3>
      <p>Filtered water with mineral support, whole-food meals, real protein. No supplement protocol survives a depleted diet.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

